course: dictionary
lesson: 3491
title: Fantasy: real or imagined?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is right. Fantasy is a good example. «Hana reads thick fantasy books alone every break.» Here fantasy is a kind of story, full of magic, dragons, wizards or imaginary worlds.
explain: Now look at this: «Cartoon cavemen who grunt and ride dinosaurs are pure fantasy.» Cavemen riding dinosaurs did not really happen, so fantasy means something made up, not real. Ask yourself: could this really happen?
explain: Fantasy can also mean a pleasant daydream, something you imagine that is not likely to come true. Fantasy football is a game where you pick an imaginary team of real players and score points from their real results. The word stays the same, but the clues in the sentence show you which meaning to use.
fact: Fantasy can mean a kind of story with magic, dragons, wizards or imaginary worlds.
fact: Fantasy can also mean something imagined or not real, like «pure fantasy».
fact: A fantasy is a pleasant daydream that is not likely to really happen.
fact: Fantasy football is a game where you pick an imaginary team of real players and score points from their results.
fact: Books like The Hobbit, Harry Potter and Narnia are fantasy books.
exercise: «Hana reads thick fantasy books alone every break.» What kind of books are these? | Lists of shopping and prices | *Stories with magic, dragons and imaginary worlds | Books of real facts about science | Maps of the school grounds
exercise: «Cartoon cavemen who grunt and ride dinosaurs are pure fantasy.» What does fantasy mean here? | *Something imagined that is not real | Something that is really true | A type of school lunch | A famous painter from long ago
exercise: Mia's fantasy is to score the winning goal at Wembley one day, but she has never even played for a team. What is a fantasy in this sentence? | A map of the school | A rule of the game | A new pair of boots | *A pleasant daydream that is not likely to come true
test: Ben picks real footballers for an imaginary team and scores points from their matches. What game is he playing? | Chess | Snap | Hide and seek | *Fantasy football
test: «It's just a fantasy» means what? | A true story from history | A new school for the children | *It is only a dream and not real | A fast race around the track
exam: The word fantasy has more than one meaning, so what should you check before you choose? | The first letter only | The length of the word | Whether the word rhymes with another word | *The clues in the sentence, such as magic or dragons, and whether it could really happen
